course: dictionary
lesson: 1812
title: Cluck, cluck: hens and fussing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hen clucks when she makes her short, low, repeated sound. Cluck can also be something people do. In «Mum clucked her tongue», Mum is not a hen: the words around cluck tell you she made a clicking sound with her tongue, which shows she was unhappy or worried.
explain: Look at the words after cluck to find its meaning. In «cluck over the baby», the baby is being looked after in a worried, caring way, just like a mother hen with her chicks. So clucking over someone means fussing over them.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. In «A broody hen ... keeps her eggs warm for about three weeks, and before hatching the chicks peep inside the shell and the hen clucks back», clucks must be a sound, because the hen is answering the chicks.
fact: Cluck is a verb and a noun: a hen clucks, and a hen makes a cluck.
fact: «Clucked her tongue» means made a clicking sound with the tongue to show she disapproved, was sorry or was worried.
fact: «Clucked over» means fussed over someone in a worried, caring way, like a mother hen.
fact: «A broody hen» is one that wants to sit on eggs; she keeps them warm for about three weeks until they hatch.
fact: «Cluck-cluck» is the sound a hen makes. Old US slang uses cluck for a silly or stupid person, so check the context before you decide what it means.
exercise: «A broody hen, one that wants to sit on eggs, keeps her eggs warm for about three weeks.» What is a broody hen? | *A hen that wants to sit on eggs | A hen that sings every morning | A hen that has run off the farm | A hen that is swimming in a pond
exercise: «Mum clucked her tongue when she saw the muddy boots.» What does clucked her tongue show? | Mum was a hen | *Mum was unhappy or worried | Mum wanted to go to bed | Mum was singing a happy song
exercise: «Grandma clucked over the baby all afternoon.» What does clucked over mean? | Ignored the baby completely | Sang the baby to sleep quietly | Ran off to the shops | *Fussed over the baby in a worried, caring way
test: «The hen clucked softly to her chicks.» What does clucked mean here? | *Made her short, low, repeated sound | Laid a golden egg | Slept all day in the barn | Flew off the farm
test: In «the hen's cluck woke us up», what kind of word is cluck? | To click your tongue | *The sound a hen makes, a noun | A silly person | To fuss over someone
exam: «Dad clucked his tongue at the spilt milk.» Using context, what does this most likely show? | Dad was singing a song | Dad was hungry and wanted lunch | *Dad disapproved or was unhappy about the mess | Dad was about to lay an egg
